cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Leonardo Lab in your research, please cite it using
  this metadata.
title: >-
  Leonardo Lab: A Constrained Evolutionary Search Architecture
  Operationalizing Structural Mechanics from Leonardo da Vinci's Notebooks
type: software
authors:
  - name: Leonardo Lab Contributors
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-25"
license: MIT
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/YOUR_ORG/leonardo-lab-transformer
keywords:
  - evolutionary computation
  - constrained optimization
  - cybernetics
  - systems architecture
  - history of science
  - structural mechanics
  - GASO state machine
abstract: >-
  Leonardo Lab is a high-fidelity, resource-constrained evolutionary
  search engine that operationalizes structural mechanics extracted
  from Leonardo da Vinci's scientific notebooks (Richter ed., 1888)
  as a domain-agnostic evolutionary kernel. The system integrates a
  formal ruleset genome, an 11-phase GASO state machine pipeline, and
  a persistent evolution archive enabling cumulative adaptation across
  execution sessions. Validation includes optimization of Wiener's
  cybernetic alpha-rhythm model and decoder-only transformer
  configurations.
